WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:02.879
Good morning Hank, it's Wednesday. On Monday
you explained to us that Warner Chilcott the

00:00:02.879 --> 00:00:07.260
pharmaceutical company that makes Asacol HD,
the drug that keeps you alive and well enough

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:11.630
to work, had unexpectedly and without warning
overnight raised the price of that drug by

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:16.420
more than 1200%. So you asked us to email
the CEO of Warner Chilcott, Roger Boissonneault,

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:21.369
which I did to say, you know, Roger Boissonneault
you are doing a fantastic job.

00:00:21.369 --> 00:00:26.699
In fact, Hank hold on the markets just opened.
Hank I've just acquired 100 shares of Warner

00:00:26.699 --> 00:00:30.910
Chilcott stock making me one 2 millionth the
owner of the company that's ruining your life.

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:35.050
You know why they're ruining your life? Because
Roger Boissonneault doesn't work for you or

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:38.300
the other people who have ulcerative colitis
Hank. He works for me!

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.840
Hank, if you go to Warner Chilcott's webpage
you know what's above the drugs and above

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:45.440
the company news and above the woman who is
delighted to have inexplicably found herself

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:50.540
in a field of flowers? The stock price. In
fact Hank, Warner Chilcott's website is not

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:56.981
located at warnerchilcott.com, it's located
at wcrx.com, which is Warner Chilcott's stock

00:00:56.981 --> 00:00:57.981
symbol.

00:00:57.981 --> 00:01:01.380
Hank, as you know I am a capitalist. I believe
in free and open markets. I believe when you

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:05.659
let suppliers and demanders figure out the
price for something you get better, cheaper

00:01:05.659 --> 00:01:09.490
goods and services. But, I don't believe in
unregulated free markets because that would

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:12.829
be insane. For instance, I don't believe that
Wal-Mart should be allowed to sell highly

00:01:12.829 --> 00:01:15.950
enriched Uranium. The free market is really
good at things like figuring out how much

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:19.840
air fare should cost and fueling the innovation
that makes it possible to make telephone calls

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:20.840
without wires.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:23.529
But Hank, there are some things that markets
can't do and the pharmaceutical industry is

00:01:23.529 --> 00:01:27.060
a great example of this. So Hank, if I were
to ask you whether you would rather have a

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:31.079
single pill that cures malaria or a single
pill that cures male pattern baldness, you'd

00:01:31.079 --> 00:01:34.450
probably say, you know, the malaria pill.
Right, because aside from the humanitarian

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:38.990
argument malaria is possibly the single biggest
suck on world economic productivity. Aside

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:42.179
from perhaps Call of Duty. And if we could
cure malaria there would be millions of new

00:01:42.179 --> 00:01:45.819
people who could work instead of being sick
themselves or taking care of sick kids, which

00:01:45.819 --> 00:01:50.669
would be a huge boom for the world economy.
Unfortunately, the free market can't see that

00:01:50.669 --> 00:01:55.239
because all it can see is Oh My God if we
cured baldness we would be so rich.

00:01:55.239 --> 00:01:58.859
So when pharmaceutical companies say that
their profits go back into research and development

00:01:58.859 --> 00:02:03.069
they're telling the truth, but they're researching
and developing lucrative drugs not drugs that

00:02:03.069 --> 00:02:07.750
maximize the benefit to the overall health
of the world. Hank the truth is Roger Boissonneault

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:11.090
is not in the business of providing you with
Asacol, he's in the business of providing

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:14.890
me with a return on my investment. So why
did Warner Chilcott offer you their drug for

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:18.819
50 dollars a month and then raie the price
to 620 dollars a month? Same reason crack

00:02:18.819 --> 00:02:22.969
dealers give out the first rock free and musicians
release free downloads. First, you maximize

00:02:22.969 --> 00:02:26.269
the number of customers, then you maximize
the profit.

00:02:26.269 --> 00:02:30.090
Hank, the great thing about drugs like Asacol
HD, I mean from the perspective of a part

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:34.709
owner of Warner Chilcott, is that if you don't
find some kind of gastrointestinal anti-inflammatory,

00:02:34.709 --> 00:02:38.980
you might die. And that makes you a super
motivated customer. Hank, you can't negotiate

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:42.790
fairly with Warner Chilcott because Warner
Chilcott knows how badly you wanna stay alive.

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:46.170
That's why Asacol is, for instance, much less
expensive in Canada where Warner Chilcott

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:49.820
isn't negotiating with individuals, they're
negotiating with the entire population of

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:50.820
Canada.

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:55.180
Hank, the free market that works so well in
so many fields fails miserably at providing

00:02:55.180 --> 00:03:00.040
efficient, inexpensive, and effective health
care. As evidence I point to the fact that

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:03.870
the rational response to learning that Warner
Chilcott has Warner Chilcotted you and other

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:08.901
people with ulcerative colitis is to purchase
Warner Chilcott stock. That is insane! To

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:13.140
me that is a strong indication that the market
is not currently incentivizing good health.

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:16.620
Hank, the real reason the United States needs
universal health insurance with good prescription

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:20.420
drug coverage is not ultimately because it's
the right thing to do, but because a healthier

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:24.930
work force that spends its capital not on
Asacol but on innovation and finding efficiencies

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:29.010
in various industries will benefit the American
economy. And Hank, I speak as an owner of

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:32.740
the company when I say that if Warner Chilcott
can't compete, if they can't deliver real

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:38.030
drugs that help real people at a fairly negotiated
price, than it can go Warner Chilcott itself.

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:38.920
Hank I'll see you on Friday.

